Hi Juan,

Thanks for testing SegOptim.

If everything went fine with the package installation and if OTB is already installed in your machine (see instructions here <https://segoptim.bitbucket.io/docs/installation.html#installing-third-party-software-for-image-segmentation>), then you need to load the package to use it. To do this run the following lines of R code (change the file paths accordingly):

library(SegOptim)

# Folder with Orfeo Toolbox binaries - change this according to your setup
otbPath <- "C:/OTB/bin"

# Path to your Sentinel-2 multiband image - change this
inputSegFeat.path <- "C:/Users/MyName/MyFiles/S2a_img_L1C.tif"

# Output segmented raster - change this too
outSegmRst.path <- "C:/Users/MyName/MyFiles/segmentedRaster.tif"

## Run OTB segmentation
outSegmRst <- segmentation_OTB_LSMS(

                      inputRstPath = inputSegFeat.path,
                      SpectralRange = 3.1,

                      SpatialRange = 4.5,
                      MinSize = 21,
                      outputSegmRst = outSegmRst.path,
                      verbose = TRUE,
                      otbBinPath = otbPath,
                      lsms_maxiter = 50)

# Check the file paths with outputs
print(outSegmRst)

# Load the segmented raster and plot it
segmRst <- raster(outSegmRst$segm)

plot(segmRst)

Try it and let us know if this works for you.
Cheers,
João
